            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the NOHrD Sprintbok worth it compared with the AssaultRunner Pro?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                As a running machine they are similar: comparable surfaces and ratings, no motor, no resistance setting. The AssaultRunner Pro costs about $3,499 with a longer frame warranty. The Sprintbok’s extra cost buys wood, craftsmanship and appearance, which is worth it only if those matter to you.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a NOHrD Sprintbok</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">At this price, the expensive mistakes are about fit, terms and logistics rather than build quality. These are the four to avoid.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying it as a walking or desk treadmill</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A curved, self-powered belt moves when you lean forward and stops when you lean back, which makes slow walking tiring, especially while typing. If walking at a desk is the main use, a flat walking treadmill is the better tool, whatever accessories are offered.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Not registering the warranty</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">NOHrD’s US warranty is one year unless you register within the first year, which extends it to two. On a machine costing over $8,000, register as soon as it arrives and keep the proof of purchase.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Underestimating delivery</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The Sprintbok arrives as one 160 kg package, delivered to the kerb. Plan the route indoors, measure doorways and stairs, and line up several people or a mover before delivery day. Damage has to be reported within 24 hours.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying for the Pro you will not use</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The Pro’s touchscreen costs $700 to $900 more. If you already train with a phone or tablet app, the V2’s display and app sync give you most of the same, and the running is identical.</p>
